quran[5]{c,v,t}:
  5,46,"And following in their footsteps, We sent ‘Isa, the son of Maryam (Jesus, the son of Mary), confirming what was before him of the Torah. We gave him the Injil (the Gospel), containing guidance and light, confirming what was (revealed) before him in the Torah—a guidance and admonition for the God-conscious."
  5,47,"Let the People of the Injil (the Gospel) judge according to what Allah has revealed in it. Those who do not judge according to what Allah has revealed, it is they who are disobedient."
  5,48,"And We have sent down to you the Book with the truth, as a verifier of all Scriptures that had come before it and as a guardian over it. So, judge between them according to what Allah has revealed, and do not follow their desires against the truth that has come to you. For each (community) among you, We have assigned a code of law and a way of life. And if Allah had willed, He would have made you one nation, but (He wills) that He should test you in respect to what He has given you. So take the lead in all good works. To Allah shall be your return all together. Then, He will inform you about what you used to differ."
  5,49,"So judge between them according to what Allah has revealed, and do not follow their desires. And beware of them lest they (try to) tempt you away from any part of what Allah has sent down to you. But if they turn away (from your judgement), then know that Allah wants to punish them for some of their sins. And indeed, many people are disobedient."
  5,50,Is it the law of pagan ignorance that they are seeking (to be judged by)? And who is better than Allah in judgement for people of firm faith?
